diff --git a/PLUGIN_SPEC.md b/PLUGIN_SPEC.md
index bc28745..47f0657 100644
--- a/PLUGIN_SPEC.md
+++ b/PLUGIN_SPEC.md
@@ -322,6 +322,17 @@ When export keys collide, priority is **local plugin > global plugin > core**. A
 plugin can override `toPng`, `toJpg`, `toCanvas` or another exporter. Use `ctx.export.url` or
 `ctx.exports` to build that export from the existing capture.
 
+To draw the same capture with extra styles (a highlight, a watermark, text hidden), give an export
+`css`: `result.toPng({ css: '.hit{outline:3px solid #f0f}' })`. The rules apply to that export
+only, after crop and restore choose its source. They go in a cascade layer declared before any
+other in the capture, so their `!important` declarations win over every stylesheet rule (an
+inline `style` with `!important` still wins). A `beforeExport` hook can add to `options.css`, and
+`ctx.exports.canvas({ ...opts, css })` draws a styled copy beside the plain one. Select by the
+page's ids, classes, attributes and tag names. SnapDOM's own generated class names are internal
+and can change, and the clone can wrap scrolling elements, so a child combinator (`>`) may miss. CSS hides; it
+does not remove, so an SVG export still carries hidden text: redact in `resolveNode`. A raster
+`html-in-canvas` capture throws.
+
 ## Distribution
 
 ### Official plugins
